// The return-position half of the interaction-boundary narrowing (ridl §7.1).
//
// A shape the interaction boundary refuses in *parameter* position gets a
// description-first message naming what is allowed; the return position now
// gets one too, and the offending shape is consumed into an error node rather
// than being handed to the annotation parser. It used to report
// `FORM-101: expected a return type` — which says nothing about what is allowed
// — and then read `[Level; 0..8]` as this member's attribute block, so one
// mistake also drew a FORM-102 and a FORM-106 "unknown attribute key `Level`",
// the last of them rendered after unrelated files.

package diag.ridl

interface NarrowingReturns {

  /// Collection in return position.
  query listLevels(): [Level; 0..8]
}
